# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3.2.11
SPECS.append(G(M, "3.2.11", "Caching note",
 "Project-root and user CLAUDE.md are read once at session start and held, so mid-session edits neither break the cache nor apply until the next /clear, /compact or restart.",
 "edit CLAUDE.md mid-session, show it does not apply, then show it applying after /clear.",
 "after editing CLAUDE.md, reload it deliberately and verify.",
 "the cache stays intact precisely because the edit does not reach the running session [Claude Code docs, Prompt caching, 2026].",
 16, "1.5", ["State the reload rule", "Explain it from the cache layout", "Design an edit-and-verify routine"],
 "A three-step demonstration log: edit, observe no effect, reload and observe effect.",
 [
 sec("The rule", "Project-root and user-level CLAUDE.md files are read once at session start and held in memory; editing them mid-session does not invalidate the cache, but the edit also does not apply, and Claude keeps working with the version loaded at session start; the new content loads on the next `/clear`, `/compact` or restart [Claude Code docs, Prompt caching, 2026].",
  tbl(["File type", "Mid-session edit"], [["Project-root, user CLAUDE.md", "No effect until `/clear`, `/compact` or restart"], ["Nested CLAUDE.md, not yet loaded", "Takes effect when it loads"], ["Nested or `paths:` rule already loaded", "No retroactive change"]]),
  "Edit-and-assume", "You edit CLAUDE.md, ask Claude to follow the new rule and conclude the file is ignored, when it was never reloaded.", "Reload with `/clear`, `/compact` or a restart, then test.",
  "editing flow is sub-topic 3.2.3 of Module 3.2.", "edit, reload, verify."),
 sec("Why: the cache layout", "Claude Code orders each request so rarely-changing content comes first: the system prompt and tool definitions, then project context (CLAUDE.md, auto memory, unscoped rules), then the conversation. Project context changes only when a session starts or after `/clear` or `/compact`; a match is exact, so a change anywhere in the prefix recomputes everything after it [Claude Code docs, Prompt caching, 2026].",
  tbl(["Layer", "Content", "Changes when"], [["System prompt", "Core instructions, tool definitions", "Tool set changes"], ["Project context", "CLAUDE.md, auto memory, unscoped rules", "Session start, `/clear`, `/compact`"], ["Conversation", "Messages and tool results", "Every turn"]]),
  "Cache-blame", "You blame the cache for CLAUDE.md not applying and disable caching, which does not change the load rule.", "Leave caching on; reload deliberately.",
  "cache mechanics are Module 3.4.", "the load rule is the cause."),
 sec("Compaction and the reload", "Compaction reloads project context from disk, which cache-hits only if CLAUDE.md and memory are unchanged since the session started [Claude Code docs, Prompt caching, 2026]. So editing CLAUDE.md and then compacting pays a cache rebuild for the changed project context. Running `/clear` rebuilds too, with a fresh conversation.",
  tbl(["Action", "Result"], [["Edit then `/clear`", "Edit applies; fresh conversation; cache rebuilt"], ["Edit then `/compact`", "Edit applies; project context cache misses once"], ["Edit then restart", "Edit applies; cache rebuilt"]]),
  "Mid-task-reload", "You compact mid-task to apply an edit, paying a rebuild and losing detail at a bad moment.", "Batch CLAUDE.md edits and apply them at a natural break between tasks.",
  "natural breaks are covered in Module 3.1.", "reload at breaks."),
 ],
 [("When do mid-session CLAUDE.md edits apply?", "On the next `/clear`, `/compact` or restart."),
  ("Does a mid-session edit break the cache?", "No."),
  ("You edit and conclude Claude ignores the file. Name the failure mode by its exact label.", "**Edit-and-assume.**"),
  ("You disable caching to make edits apply. Name the failure mode.", "**Cache-blame.**"),
  ("You compact mid-task just to apply an edit. Name the failure mode.", "**Mid-task-reload.**"),
  ("What are the three request layers in order?", "System prompt, project context, conversation."),
  ("When does an unloaded nested CLAUDE.md edit take effect?", "When it loads on demand."),
  ("After a compaction, when does project context cache-hit?", "Only if CLAUDE.md and memory are unchanged since the session started."),
  ("Which layers does a conversation change leave cached?", "System prompt and project context.")],
 [("Start a session and note the rule in CLAUDE.md", "Baseline"), ("Edit the rule and ask Claude to follow it", "Observation 1"), ("Run `/clear` and repeat", "Observation 2"), ("Write the three-layer cache diagram", "Diagram"),
  ("Edit a nested file before it loads and test", "Observation 3"), ("Write your edit routine", "Routine")],
 ["Step", "Expected", "Observed"], [["Edit mid-session", "Old behaviour", "Old behaviour"], ["After `/clear`", "New behaviour", "New behaviour"], ["Nested before load", "New behaviour", "New behaviour"]],
 [["Only one observation", "Rule unproven"], ["Caching disabled to test", "**Cache-blame**"]],
 "The artifact passes only if the old and new behaviour were both observed.",
 [["Anthropic", "Prompt caching", "Editing CLAUDE.md mid-session; layers", "Current"], ["Anthropic", "Memory", "Doc gap on mid-session edits", "Current"]],
 "the Memory page does not say whether mid-session edits apply; the Prompt caching page states they do not until reload.",
 "This is the craft of reloading: **edit, reload, verify.** The engineer who understands this does not ask \"why is it ignoring my edit?\" — they ask \"has this session loaded it yet?\""))

